From: OpenAI <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: realtek: align extension mode mask with value

Each extension mode occupies four bits. EXT1 is bits 7:4 of 0x1305,
whereas EXT0 uses bits 3:0 and EXT2 uses bits 3:0 of 0x13c3. The value
already uses a nibble offset, but the mask shifts by only one bit for
EXT1. This leaves stale EXT1 mode bits and clears part of EXT0 instead.

The RTL8367C SDK and all three archived OEM kernels use 0xf << (id * 4)
for EXT0/EXT1. Use the existing offset macro for both mask and value.
The RTL8367D-specific EXT1 path already uses GENMASK(7, 4).

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb.c
@@ -218,3 +218,3 @@
 #define   RTL8365MB_DIGITAL_INTERFACE_SELECT_MODE_MASK(_extint) \
-		(0xF << (((_extint) % 2)))
+		(0xF << RTL8365MB_DIGITAL_INTERFACE_SELECT_MODE_OFFSET(_extint))
 #define   RTL8365MB_DIGITAL_INTERFACE_SELECT_MODE_OFFSET(_extint) \
